  ('4.14.20.4.5', 'Conduct a 5-day residential workshop with 40 participants to develop a standardized training curriculum for all laboratory staff. Covering relevant topics like specific laboratory techniques for priority diseases, biosafety and biosecurity protocols, sample management, referral and simple laboratory data analysis', 25599000.00::numeric, 565),
  ('4.14.20.4.6', 'Conduct a 4-day comprehensive needs assessment (2 days for checklist development & 2 days for assessment) by 20 Assessors for 30 HFs (5 per zone) to evaluate the existing infrastructure, laboratory equipment, and supply chain systems to support priority disease testing (Malaria, Diphtheria, Measles, Cholera & Mpox)', 6000000.00::numeric, 566),
